Package: DirectoR
Title: Launch and Teaser Films for Apps and Websites
Version: 0.1.3
Authors@R: c(
    person("DirectoR", "maintainers", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "director@example.org"))
Description: A Shiny studio that directs short launch and teaser films (under 60
    seconds) for web apps, Shiny apps and websites. Paste a link, a Git repository
    or a zip of the source: DirectoR launches the app, explores it in a headless
    browser, learns its name, tagline, logo and colours, writes a storyboard and a
    voice-over script, records real interactions as perfectly smooth 60 fps
    footage, composes original music and sound design, and cuts the film with
    kinetic typography, camera moves and transitions. Outputs MP4 (16:9, 9:16,
    1:1, 4:5), burned-in captions, SRT, a poster and the script. The film engine
    (bundled in inst/engine) is written in Python and drives Chromium through
    Playwright and ffmpeg.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Language: en-GB
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports:
    bslib (>= 0.5.0),
    htmltools,
    jsonlite,
    processx (>= 3.5.0),
    shiny (>= 1.7.0),
    tools,
    stats,
    utils,
    grDevices
Suggests:
    ps,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: Python (>= 3.9) with numpy, scipy, pillow and playwright
    (Chromium); ffmpeg with libx264 (libass for burned-in captions); git for
    repositories; optional voices: macOS say, edge-tts, piper-tts, ttspico,
    espeak-ng, OpenAI or ElevenLabs API keys.
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
